    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d170">

                <pb facs="0258" n="246" sameAs="frus:frus1944v03/pg246"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">841D.01/292: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Ireland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gray</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-04-04T20:00:00-04:00">April 4, 1944—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>56. Below is the text of a further note which we propose to send to Prime
                    Minister de Valera. Although the draft had been prepared before the receipt of
                    your telegram no. 59, March 21,<anchor n="38" xml:id="d170-f1"/> we have added
                    to it certain suggestions from your telegram. Please telegraph any comments you
                    have on this note. This draft is being telegraphed to Winant today for clearance
                    with the British. As soon as the British approval is received we shall telegraph
                    you. We believe it would be better for you to send the note rather than to
                    deliver it in person. We plan to give this note to the press as soon as you
                    telegraph that it has been delivered. The text of the note follows as Department
                    No. 57.<anchor n="39" xml:id="d170-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
